<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia SEM ray angles (Pass 1) (Grantia aff. indica Dendy, 1913 (Porifera: Calcarea), ZMA Por. 11556b)",
        "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia SEM ray angles (Pass 1) faithfully reproduces Grantia aff. indica Dendy, 1913 (Porifera: Calcarea), ZMA Por. 11556b morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-024-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-024-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-024-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-024-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-024-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Grantia aff. indica Dendy, 1913 (Porifera: Calcarea), ZMA Por. 11556b specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py> ;
    schema:about "Grantia aff. indica Dendy, 1913 (Porifera: Calcarea), ZMA Por. 11556b" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does NOT claim a verdict in Pass 1: the paired-difference statistic has no null distribution yet (R2).",
        "does_not_claim: Does NOT claim the mechanism (passive deposition between arbitrary neighbouring cells) is correct: Ledger & Jones (1977) and Voigt et al. (2017) show a dedicated sclerocyte sextet; only the geometric content (ray axes obey a tension-triangle force balance of the secreting cell group) is tested.",
        "does_not_claim: Does NOT use the pre-assigned Dryad dataset (hexactine fossil tomograms, 5.8 GB): recorded as DATASET_MISMATCH, metadata pinned.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Neumann law of cosines in integer-exact form (E3), sagittal one-parameter family (E5) and its inverse, tetrahedral/orthogonal constants, radial-arc ray-angle extraction on one CC BY SEM plate of Grantia aff. indica (8 three-ray spicules, 3 monaxons), per-spicule rho fit, side-by-side renders, layered growth animation.",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson (1917, pp. 443-449) argues, after Dreyer (1892) and Plateau (1873), that calcareous spicule rays follow the junction lines of 3 or 4 contiguous cells: 120 deg when tensions are equal, 'two equal angles and one unequal' when not, tetrahedral ~109 deg for four cells; the spicule is 'a crystal under restraint'.",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson gives drawings (Fig. 214, after Haeckel) and no measured angle table.",
        "transfer_boundary: One plate, one individual, one genus; 2D projection of trihedral spicules; tetractine apical ray not measurable (P3 untestable here); no alcyonarian spicules at all although the claim text names them." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py; output: docs/media/t1917_024_on_concretions_spicules_and_sp_comparison.png; organism: Grantia aff. indica Dendy, 1913 (Porifera: Calcarea), ZMA Por. 11556b; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Thompson (1917, pp. 443-449) argues, after Dreyer (1892) and Plateau (1873), that calcareous spicule rays follow the junction lines of 3 or 4 contiguous cells: 120 deg when tensions are equal, 'two equal angles and one unequal' when not, tetrahedral ~109 deg for four cells; the spicule is 'a crystal under restraint'. | Thompson gives drawings (Fig. 214, after Haeckel) and no measured angle table.; reconstructed_in_script: Neumann law of cosines in integer-exact form (E3), sagittal one-parameter family (E5) and its inverse, tetrahedral/orthogonal constants, radial-arc ray-angle extraction on one CC BY SEM plate of Grantia aff. indica (8 three-ray spicules, 3 monaxons), per-spicule rho fit, side-by-side renders, layered growth animation.; transfer_boundary: One plate, one individual, one genus; 2D projection of trihedral spicules; tetractine apical ray not measurable (P3 untestable here); no alcyonarian spicules at all although the claim text names them.; does_not_claim: Does NOT claim the mechanism (passive deposition between arbitrary neighbouring cells) is correct: Ledger & Jones (1977) and Voigt et al. (2017) show a dedicated sclerocyte sextet; only the geometric content (ray axes obey a tension-triangle force balance of the secreting cell group) is tested. | Does NOT claim a verdict in Pass 1: the paired-difference statistic has no null distribution yet (R2). | Does NOT use the pre-assigned Dryad dataset (hexactine fossil tomograms, 5.8 GB): recorded as DATASET_MISMATCH, metadata pinned.]; other sources: On Growth and Form (Ch. IX: On Concretions, Spicules, and Spicular Skeletons, pp. 411-487, Figs. 194-235) <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00221776>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jsb.2016.04.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/srep45658>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.190911>,
        <https://doi.org/10.11646/zootaxa.4426.1.1> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-024-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-024-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-024-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-024-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-024-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-024-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-024-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-024-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-024-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-024-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-024-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-024-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-024-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-024-7> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Surface-Tension Force Balance at a Plateau Border (Neumann Tension Triangle) & Polyhedral Ray Geometry" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 6.23e-01 .

