<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia SEM ray angles (Pass 1) — Code-to-model traceability: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring states P1-P3 and E1-E8 with Thompson page numbers; every model function's docstring names its equation; the Lean header maps each theorem to an equation and to script function names; the KG yaml links code loci by function name. Deductions: code loci are by function name, not line range; the segmentation thresholds (90, 400, 1500, fill 0.9) are not traced to anything but the plate." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia SEM ray angles (Pass 1) — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The force balance, law of cosines, equiangular point, sagittal family and its inverse, tetrahedral and orthogonal limits and the interstice area are implemented exactly as Thompson states them and six Lean theorems check the algebra (equiangular iff c = m via the factorisation 2cm(c-m)(c+2m); ordering and T-limit; tetrahedral by decide). Deductions: Thompson's own mechanism is adsorption/deposition along Plateau borders of a cell FOAM — the script never simulates a foam or a cell doublet, it only uses the junction force balance; ray curvature (Fig. 214 C) and non-planarity (p. 444) are outside the model; the growth GIF's three-cell field is illustrative, not derived from the tensions." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py L296–L307: three_cell_field places cells on sector bisectors — illustrative, not a tension-derived doublet geometry <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0643f406e28a6ba3f9600caef4642142fc8be064/thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py#L296-L307>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia SEM ray angles (Pass 1) — Morphometric validation: 48/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Identical ray-axis morphometrics are measured on every real spicule (near-junction and chord axes, three angles, paired difference, unpaired deviation, fitted rho) and summarised in measure_morphoeval (median paired difference 4.2 deg vs unpaired deviation 27 deg). Deductions: n = 8 from one plate; no null distribution for the paired difference (a random partition of 360 deg also has a smallest gap); no goodness-of-fit (r, RMSE, KS) against the model; no second specimen population and Thompson's Fig. 214 is pinned but not digitised; near- vs chord-axis sensitivity is recorded but not analysed; measurement error from projection is unquantified." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py L438–L462: measure_morphoeval: summary statistics, no null, no GoF <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0643f406e28a6ba3f9600caef4642142fc8be064/thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py#L438-L462>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-all-ray-angles-sd>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-closest-pair-angle-difference-median>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-fitted-tension-ratio-rho-range>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-interstice-area-coefficient-e9>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-tetrahedral-inter-ray-angle-e7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-three-ray-spicules-measured-on-the-sem-plate>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-unpaired-angle-deviation-from-the-paired-angle-mean>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 4.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia SEM ray angles (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 62.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Neumann tension triangle (E1-E3) with the equiangular point (E4), the one-parameter sagittal family cos(theta_pair) = -rho/2 (E5), tetrahedral/orthogonal limits (E7/E8) and the curvilinear interstice (E9); six Lean theorems kernel-checked. Radial-arc ray extraction on the SEM plate finds 8 three-ray spicules and 3 monaxons (self-tested). Angles: all-angle SD 15.5 deg; closest-pair difference median 4.2 deg (mean 5.7); unpaired deviation mean 27.0 deg; ratio 4.7; fitted rho spans 0.37 (T-shaped atrial tetractine) to 1.43 (Y-shaped cortical triactine); 3/8 spicules equiangular within 10 deg. Verdict is withheld until Pass 2 adds a null control: in Pass 1 the small paired difference has no reference distribution. Overall (weighted) 62.3/100. Overall 62.3/100 (faithfulness 58.0, reproducibility 72.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0643f406e28a6ba3f9600caef4642142fc8be064; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 58, Parameter expressivity 45, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 82, Code-to-model traceability 70, Reproducibility package 66. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_024_on_concretions_spicules_and_sp_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py at 0643f406e28a6ba3f9600caef4642142fc8be064, image/png, 324123 B, 1870×792 px, artifact_sha256 3f92607c5d3f21ac06d4baaf5982288625f9ce76cc2ef37224d4943b1763e6fc (sha256 3f92607c5d3f21ac06d4baaf5982288625f9ce76cc2ef37224d4943b1763e6fc), spec_fingerprint 77e8201d27dd51cb520268fe921b47c6a9cc21b65c7f28e750eaa978978c6f12. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 77e8201d27dd51cb520268fe921b47c6a9cc21b65c7f28e750eaa978978c6f12; artifact_sha256: 3f92607c5d3f21ac06d4baaf5982288625f9ce76cc2ef37224d4943b1763e6fc; input_dataset_sha256: {dryad_8mv00jv_dataset_metadata.json=8b1273b453ccdb77..., grantia_indica_zootaxa4426_fig53_sem.jpg=70194abe78894820..., grantia_spicules_readey_100x.jpg=08641621770534e1..., thompson1917_fig214_ia_leaf465_p445.jpg=019168c1fa4adddc...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917, pp. 443-449) argues, after Dreyer (1892) and Plateau (1873), that calcareous spicule rays follow the junction lines of 3 or 4 contiguous cells: 120 deg when tensions are equal, 'two equal angles and one unequal' when not, tetrahedral ~109 deg for four cells; the spicule is 'a crystal under restraint'. | Thompson gives drawings (Fig. 214, after Haeckel) and no measured angle table.; reconstructed_in_script: Neumann law of cosines in integer-exact form (E3), sagittal one-parameter family (E5) and its inverse, tetrahedral/orthogonal constants, radial-arc ray-angle extraction on one CC BY SEM plate of Grantia aff. indica (8 three-ray spicules, 3 monaxons), per-spicule rho fit, side-by-side renders, layered growth animation.; transfer_boundary: One plate, one individual, one genus; 2D projection of trihedral spicules; tetractine apical ray not measurable (P3 untestable here); no alcyonarian spicules at all although the claim text names them.; does_not_claim: Does NOT claim the mechanism (passive deposition between arbitrary neighbouring cells) is correct: Ledger & Jones (1977) and Voigt et al. (2017) show a dedicated sclerocyte sextet; only the geometric content (ray axes obey a tension-triangle force balance of the secreting cell group) is tested. | Does NOT claim a verdict in Pass 1: the paired-difference statistic has no null distribution yet (R2). | Does NOT use the pre-assigned Dryad dataset (hexactine fossil tomograms, 5.8 GB): recorded as DATASET_MISMATCH, metadata pinned.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor (different provider) — this round is builder-scored'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': \"Null control for the paired-difference statistic: Monte Carlo Dirichlet(1,1,1) random partitions of 360 deg (smallest-gap distribution) with a one-sided p-value and KS test; otherwise 'two equal angles' is unsupported\"}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Parameter sweep: rho from 0 to 2 with measured outputs (angle triplets re-measured from rendered spicules by the same radial method — closes the measurement loop) and the general three-tension model'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': \"Second specimen population: segment the CC BY-SA Grantia micrograph (many free triradiates) for the P1 120-deg mode, and digitise Thompson's own Fig. 214 (pinned IA leaf 465) with the same method\"}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Goodness-of-fit: Pearson r and RMSE of model-predicted vs measured angle triplets, CV of angles, near-axis vs chord-axis sensitivity'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'Fix the basal-ray orientation heuristic for rho > 1 spicules and render the tetractine apical ray / ray curvature honestly (or state the limit)'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R7', 'item': \"Ablation control: a 'crystallographic' alternative (Haeckel's view Thompson argues against — discrete 60/90/120 deg axes) vs the continuous E5 family, scored on the same data\"}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R8', 'item': 'Expose rho, threshold and radial parameters on the CLI; silence/upgrade the scikit-image deprecations'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 6.23e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia SEM ray angles (Pass 1) — Parameter expressivity: 45/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "rho is the single morphospace parameter and it monotonically moves the form from T (rho 0) through equiangular (rho 1) towards detachment (rho 2); the GIF shows three values and the angle-plane panel draws the whole curve. But there is no sweep with measured outputs, no CLI control of rho, threshold or radial parameters, no exploration of the general three-tension model (gamma_1, gamma_2, gamma_3 free), and the (pair, unpaired) plane is tautological (sum = 360) so the curve conveys nothing the sorted angles do not already contain." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py L393–L414: angle-plane panel; points on the line by construction (labelled as such) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0643f406e28a6ba3f9600caef4642142fc8be064/thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py#L393-L414>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-parameter-expressivity-1> ;
