<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia SEM ray angles (Pass 1) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 58/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Side by side, each measured spicule (ray axes re-rendered) is matched by the E5 model at its fitted rho: the Y-shaped cortical triactine (rho 1.43), the sagittal tubar triactines (rho ~0.74) and the T-shaped atrial tetractine (rho 0.37) are all visibly reproduced; the SEM overlay shows the detected axes on the real spicules. Deductions: the model panel for the rho > 1 spicule is mis-oriented (basal-ray picker), rays are drawn straight and tapered while the real laterals of c and e curve, the tetractines' apical ray is not rendered, and only one specimen image is compared." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py L423–L435: _basal_dir orientation heuristic; wrong for the rho > 1 (Y) spicule in the rendered panel <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0643f406e28a6ba3f9600caef4642142fc8be064/thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py#L423-L435>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-specimen-match-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

